/target
**/*.rs.bk
*.pt
*.npz
/data
__pycache__/

# Expanded .shard files are hundreds of MB for a real run (3000 games ~ 427MB)
# and GitHub hard-rejects anything over 100MB, so they never get committed.
# The glob also covers the staging directories used to hold a corpus out of an
# experiment without deleting it.
selfplay-data*/**/*.shard
selfplay-data*/**/*.bin

# Compact .gamelog files are the opposite case: ~23MB per 3000 games, which is
# the whole point of that format — several machines pooling their self-play
# through the repository. They are deliberately NOT ignored.
!selfplay-data/
!selfplay-data/*.gamelog
